### Sahar API — IntelliJ IDEA HTTP Client (Ultimate).
### Start the app (./mvnw spring-boot:run), then click the green ▶ next to any request.
### On the free tier you can still read this file as a map of the whole API.
### Docs: see reference/intellij-ultimate.md in the repo.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### The whole routine (everything the home page renders)
GET {{host}}/api/config
Accept: application/json

### Current prayer times
GET {{host}}/api/prayer-times

### Replace prayer times (idempotent PUT)
PUT {{host}}/api/prayer-times
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fajr": "04:37", "sunrise": "05:59", "dhuhr": "12:37",
  "asr": "17:12", "maghrib": "19:13", "isha": "20:36",
  "methodNote": "edited in the HTTP Client"
}

### Validation demo — a malformed time should return HTTP 400 with a clear message
PUT {{host}}/api/prayer-times
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fajr": "24:99", "sunrise": "05:59", "dhuhr": "12:37", "asr": "17:12", "maghrib": "19:13", "isha": "20:36" }

### Calculate prayer times for a location (Karachi 18°, Hanafi Asr) — does NOT save
### tz is MINUTES east of UTC (IST = 330). Tweak lat/lng/tz and re-run.
GET {{host}}/api/prayer-times/calculate?lat=19.22&lng=72.98&tz=330

### Geocode: search a place name
GET {{host}}/api/geocode?q=Thane

### Reverse geocode: name for a point
GET {{host}}/api/geocode/reverse?lat=19.22&lng=72.98

### Current location
GET {{host}}/api/location

### Set the location (used to compute prayer times)
PUT {{host}}/api/location
Content-Type: application/json

{ "placeName": "Thane, Maharashtra, India", "lat": 19.22, "lng": 72.98, "tzOffset": 330 }

### Change the month label
PUT {{host}}/api/month
Content-Type: application/json

{ "month": "July 2026" }

### The training block
GET {{host}}/api/block

### Roll the block forward to next month's template
POST {{host}}/api/block/roll-forward

### Add an accumulation week (kept before the deload; max 5 weeks)
POST {{host}}/api/block/weeks

### Edit one week (deload stays positional, so it isn't in the body)
PUT {{host}}/api/block/weeks/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Foundation", "startDate": "1 Jul", "endDate": "7 Jul", "trainingFocus": "easy week", "backendFocus": "Spring core" }

### The daily timeline
GET {{host}}/api/schedule

### Create a timeline slot (201 Created; id is assigned by the DB)
POST {{host}}/api/schedule
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": null, "time": "06:30", "title": "Test slot", "detail": "added via HTTP Client", "category": "work", "dayType": "weekday" }

### The weekly meal plan
GET {{host}}/api/diet-plan

### Edit one day's meals (Mon..Sun)
PUT {{host}}/api/diet-plan/Mon
Content-Type: application/json

{ "lunch": "Mutton keema + greens", "dinner": "Grilled bangda", "note": "edited via HTTP Client" }
